    pr_ref:  # a631
    description: "**Defect.** A documented `limits.skipped_languages` field has a setter with zero callers, so it is always empty even when its documented trigger condition occurs.\n\n**Evidence.** `limits.skipped_languages` is documented (spec §184: \"If a specific grammar fails to load, that language is skipped with explicit limits.skipped_languages[] logging\"; spec §957) to log languages skipped because their grammar failed to load. Its only writer is `add_skipped_language` (limits.py:114-117). A grep across all packages/*/src/ for callers of `add_skipped_language` (and any other write to skipped_languages) returns ZERO hits. The field is `[]` in the map. A sibling field for the different \"no files matched\" condition (limits.skipped_passes) does work (66 entries) — only the grammar-load-failure field is dead.\n\n**Contract.** The setter should be wired into the grammar-load-failure path, so a grammar that fails to load appears in `skipped_languages` as the spec describes.\n\n**Consequence.** The field always reports \"no languages skipped,\" even when grammar loading fails — a silent false assurance that every detected language was analyzed."  # a631
    fields: {}  # a631
